WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.420
Fleet tools need credentials by name, and

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:06.591
they need somewhere sensible to keep them.

00:00:06.591 --> 00:00:12.111
Lazarette Lite is the light answer:
a browser window on the Windows

00:00:12.111 --> 00:00:16.575
Credential Manager you already have,
with no new vault.

00:00:16.575 --> 00:00:20.651
This is a short run,
using throwaway credentials only.

00:00:21.401 --> 00:00:24.933
Lazarette Lite is a browser window
on the Windows Credential Manager.

00:00:24.933 --> 00:00:30.217
Double-click the launcher, and a small
PowerShell server starts on this computer.

00:00:30.917 --> 00:00:35.890
The server listens on loopback only,
on a port Windows picks.

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:40.000
It answers only your own Windows user's
processes, with a one-time launch token
